EVE University Wiki (CC BY-SA 4.0)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Some reference text and the mechanics cited in source-code comments and tool
descriptions (for example "Stacking penalties", "Capacitor", "Propulsion equipment")
are taken or condensed from the EVE University Wiki, https://wiki.eveuniversity.org/,
(c) EVE University and its wiki contributors, available under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/ . The text was shortened, reformatted
and combined with other material; it is not endorsed by EVE University. Derived text
remains under CC BY-SA 4.0 (share-alike) and is kept apart from the code licence. Tool
results that use wiki text name the page in their sources.

The ice-belt dataset icebelts/ice_systems.json lists the highsec and lowsec systems
that the EVE University Wiki pages "Clear Icicle Belt", "White Glaze Belt", "Blue Ice
Belt" and "Glacial Mass Belt" name (https://wiki.eveuniversity.org/Ice_harvesting),
(c) EVE University and its wiki contributors, CC BY-SA 4.0. It was extracted and
checked against the SDE; the file stays under CC BY-SA 4.0 and is not covered by the
MIT licence. Tool results that use it (find_systems, get_system_info) name the source
in their attribution.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Community fit sources
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The community-fit search returns fits that community sites publish (for example
EVE Workbench, Abyss Tracker, and similar). The fits are not bundled with this
repository and not redistributed in bulk: they are served by a running API with the
source, link-back and licence on every hit. Respect each site's terms if you run your
own index.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EvE-Scout (Thera and Turnur connections)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

get_thera_connections shows live wormhole connections from Thera and Turnur read from
EvE-Scout's public API, https://api.eve-scout.com/v2/public/signatures, scanning data
by EvE-Scout / Signal Cartel, https://www.eve-scout.com/ . The API publishes no terms;
it is used with attribution, a descriptive User-Agent and at most one request per cache
lifetime. Results name EvE-Scout / Signal Cartel as their source. Character names in the
API answer are not read, kept or shown. The data is not endorsed by EvE-Scout.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pyfa (validation reference only)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The reference numbers in testdata/golden/gofa/oracle/ were produced by running Pyfa
(https://github.com/pyfa-org/Pyfa, GPL-3.0, with the eos component partly under LGPL) as
a separate local test oracle. The files contain attribute values from Fenris Creations'
data and numbers computed from them; no Pyfa or eos source code, data file or binary is
included in, imported by or linked with this software. Gofa is compared against these
numbers in tests only.

